{#
  One entry of a role's `k8s_claims`, rendered by k8s/manifests as `claim-<name>.yaml` in the
  role's own manifest directory. This is the only template that renders a PersistentVolumeClaim
  (#3387). `manifests_claim` is the loop variable that task sets; it is
  `{name, size, storage_class}`, every key required (k8s/manifests asserts the shape first),
  plus two optional keys:

    access_modes   defaults to `['ReadWriteOnce']`. media-volume's `media-data` passes
                   `['ReadWriteMany']`; a claim's access modes are immutable once created, so
                   this must match the live claim.
    namespace      defaults to the shared `k8s_namespace`. observability's four claims (loki,
                   prometheus, grafana, tempo) pass `k8s_observability_namespace`.

  A claim's WHY (its storage class, its backup posture) differs role to role, so it sits beside
  the role's own `*_storage_class` / `*_size` default rather than here: valheim's nobackup
  install claim and pi-peer-backup's "Plain `longhorn` ON PURPOSE (not -nobackup)" both do this.

  The last value carries its own newline so the file ends in a blank line, the bytes the retired
  `pvc()` macro rendered. Without it every claim role's `manifests_digest` moves on a change that
  alters no object. A literal blank line would not survive the end-of-file-fixer hook.
#}
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: {{ manifests_claim.name }}
  namespace: {{ manifests_claim.namespace | default(k8s_namespace, true) }}
spec:
  accessModes:
    - {{ manifests_claim.access_modes | default(['ReadWriteOnce'], true) | join('\n    - ') }}
  storageClassName: {{ manifests_claim.storage_class }}
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: {{ manifests_claim.size ~ '\n' }}
